TextMorph for SwiftUI
=====================

This package is a native SwiftUI port of Torph, a dependency-free animated text
component for the web.

    Torph: https://torph.lochie.me
    https://github.com/lochie/torph
    Copyright (c) 2025 Lochie Axon
    Licensed under the MIT License

The morph engine (Sources/TextMorph/Core) is a direct port of Torph's
packages/torph/src/lib: the text segmentation in text-morph/utils/segment.ts,
the place-value number segmentation in text-morph/utils/number.ts, the segment
diff in text-morph/utils/diff.ts, the longest common subsequence in
utils/lcs.ts, the animation timing in text-morph/utils/animate.ts,
number-animate.ts and replace-animate.ts, and the spring and easing solvers in
utils/spring.ts and utils/easing.ts.

Test fixtures under Tests/TextMorphTests/Fixtures are generated from the
published npm package so this port can be verified against upstream output.
